WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.050 --> 00:00:02.888
Here's what you'll be able to
do by the end of this module,

2
00:00:02.888 --> 00:00:05.275
which takes about sixty
minutes with the lab.

3
00:00:05.275 --> 00:00:08.800
You'll name the four dispositions
a Kerberos account can have,

4
00:00:08.800 --> 00:00:10.113
and what each one needs.

5
00:00:10.113 --> 00:00:14.553
You'll explain why a D M S A can't be
used for a managed service account,

6
00:00:14.553 --> 00:00:17.863
or for an account with
unconstrained delegation.

7
00:00:17.863 --> 00:00:22.863
You'll read the plan, the island list and
the reconciliation for a fictional domain.

8
00:00:22.863 --> 00:00:25.419
And you'll show that the
write path runs only a

9
00:00:25.419 --> 00:00:28.113
plan whose hash was
approved, and never deletes.

10
00:00:28.113 --> 00:00:34.660
Before you start, finish Module 1, because
the lab reads Chapter 1's register, and

11
00:00:34.660 --> 00:00:40.703
Module 3, where the matrix sends Kerberos-only
accounts to a G M S A or a D M S A.

12
00:00:40.703 --> 00:00:45.538
Lab 1 needs PowerShell 7.1 or
later with Pester 5, and a clone.

13
00:00:45.538 --> 00:00:46.510
No tenant.
